              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to David I. Bruck, bruck noted that only a small minority of states treat future dangerousness as a statutory aggravating factor."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Waters",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a56afe33ea862db543b1d8f3cd6066e3bd0b04bcd13b98c00488ca17f20add19",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a56afe33ea86-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Waters, mr.\u202fWaters explained that Simmons v. South Carolina created a limited due\u2011process exception allowing juries to consider future dangerousness, and that the prosecution must raise that issue to overcome the state rule."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner \u2013 William Arthur Kelly",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
